"documents": {
"0000123456-25-000040/ex99-1.htm": "<html><body><p>Example Semi reports third quarter 2025 results. Revenue for the third quarter of 2025 was $1.90 billion, up 12% year over year. Gross margin was 55.2%. Diluted earnings per share were $1.10. Outlook: for the fourth quarter of 2025, the company expects revenue between $1.95 billion and $2.05 billion, gross margin between 55% and 57%, and diluted EPS between $1.15 and $1.25.</p></body></html>",
"0000123456-26-000005/ex99-1.htm": "<html><body><p>Example Semi reports fourth quarter and full year 2025 results. Revenue for the fourth quarter of 2025 was $2.08 billion. Gross margin was 56.1%. Diluted earnings per share were $1.22. For the first quarter of 2026 the company expects revenue between $2.00 billion and $2.10 billion, gross margin between 55% and 57%, and diluted EPS between $1.20 and $1.30. The company expects capital expenditures for fiscal 2026 of approximately $1.5 billion.</p></body></html>",
"0000123456-26-000031/ex99-1.htm": "<html><body><p>Example Semi reports first quarter 2026 results. Revenue for the first quarter of 2026 was $2.12 billion. Gross margin was 56.5%. Diluted earnings per share were $1.35. Outlook: for the second quarter of 2026, the company anticipates revenue in the range of $2.20 billion to $2.30 billion and gross margin between 56% and 58%.</p></body></html>",
"0000123456-26-000058/ex99-1.htm": "<html><body><p>Example Semi reports second quarter 2026 results. Revenue for the second quarter of 2026 was $2.18 billion. Gross margin was 57.0%. Diluted earnings per share were $1.28. For the third quarter of 2026 the company expects revenue between $2.40 billion and $2.50 billion and gross margin between 57% and 59%. Capital expenditures for fiscal 2026 are now expected to be approximately $1.6 billion.</p></body></html>",
"0000123456-26-000012/form10k.htm": "<html><body><p>Annual report. Item 1. Business. Customers. Sales to Customer A accounted for approximately 24% of our net revenue in 2025 and 21% in 2024. Our ten largest customers accounted for 61% of net revenue in 2025. Note 15. Segment information. One customer represented 24% of total revenue for the year ended December 31, 2025. Item 1A. Risk factors. We depend on a small number of customers.</p></body></html>"
